      "A simple way to decide: if the word you keep using is *fresh* and *cool*, start with eucalyptus-mint. If the word you keep using is *clean* and *soft*, start with coastal-linen. Either one is a legitimate, standalone Autivara scent, not a literal copy of anyone's formula — it's inspired by that overall category of fragrance, built with our own oils.",
      "## Common mistakes people make chasing a store-scent dupe",
      "The most common mistake is reaching for a single essential oil, usually straight eucalyptus, and expecting it to smell like the store. It won't. A raw essential oil is one note; the scent people are chasing is a blend of at least three or four notes working together, plus a delivery method that keeps it even and low rather than sharp. A blended fragrance oil built for exactly this purpose will get you closer in one try than weeks of mixing your own oils in a carrier.",
