      "If you want a version that also travels — a lot of people who love the Lululemon scent want it in the car on the way to and from the studio, not just at home — a [vent clip car diffuser](/product/autivora-magnetic-vent-diffuser) with the same eucalyptus-mint oil keeps the theme consistent from your house to your gym bag. It's a small detail, but matching your car scent to your home scent is exactly the kind of signature-scent consistency that made the original store smell memorable in the first place.",
      "## Layering for a more complex, boutique-level result",
      "If you want to get even closer to the multi-layered feeling of a real retail space — which almost never smells like one single note — try running your primary scent as the base and adding a second, lighter diffuser with a complementary profile in an adjoining room. Eucalyptus-mint in the main living space with coastal-linen running lightly in a bedroom or bathroom creates a sense of a scent that shifts subtly as you move through the house, rather than one flat note everywhere, which is closer to how a real store with multiple zones actually smells.",
      "This is also a good moment to remember that the whole point of a refillable system is that you can experiment. Since Autivara oils aren't locked to a single device or a subscription, you can pick up a second scent, try it for a week, and switch back with zero waste and no cartridge to throw away. [Browse the full home diffuser collection](/home) to see which hardware fits your space before committing to a scent.",
      "[[cta]]Explore the Home Collection|/home",
      "## Frequently asked questions",
      "### Does Lululemon sell its store scent as a candle or spray?",
