      "There's also a practical reason hospitality brands favor this family of notes: it performs well across large, high-ceilinged, high-traffic spaces. A crisp citrus top note can feel thin and disappear in a cavernous lobby; a warm base of amber, vanilla, and wood has enough depth to still register from across the room, which is part of why this category of scent has become something close to an industry standard for luxury hospitality generally, not just one specific brand.",
