      "### What scent works best for a musty closet once it's dry?",
      "Clean, soft, and laundry-adjacent notes work best because they reinforce the \"fresh air\" feeling rather than fighting for attention in a small enclosed space. [Coastal Linen](/scents/coastal-linen) gives a crisp, just-washed character; [Cloud Cotton](/scents/cloud-cotton) is a touch softer and closer to fresh bedding. Both hold up well at low intensity, which is what a closet needs.",
      "### How often should I use moisture absorbers in a closet?",
      "Check them on the schedule the product recommends — most calcium-chloride tubs need replacing every 30 to 60 days, faster in humid climates or during summer. A saturated absorber stops pulling moisture out of the air, so treat it as ongoing maintenance rather than a one-time fix, especially in closets on exterior walls or above unheated spaces."
